# DiMovie — Environment Variables

## apps/api (.env)

```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/dimovie
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-access-min-32-chars-long!!
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-refresh-min-32-chars-long!
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=2h
JWT_REFRESH_TTL=30d
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# Leave empty when the web app proxies API via /backend (recommended).
COOKIE_DOMAIN=
COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Cloudflare Turnstile (optional — CAPTCHA only when trust score is low)
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Cloudflare R2 (required for video file upload)
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=dimovie-uploads
R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://cdn.example.com

# Voice: Railway default is P2P + TURN (set VOICE_SFU_ENABLED=true only on hosts with UDP)
# If TURN_URLS is empty, API mints Open Relay static-auth TURN credentials automatically.
# Optional Metered: METERED_TURN_API_URL=https://<app>.metered.live/api/v1/turn/credentials?apiKey=...
VOICE_SFU_ENABLED=false
MEDIASOUP_LISTEN_IP=0.0.0.0
MEDIASOUP_ANNOUNCED_IP=
MEDIASOUP_RTC_MIN_PORT=40000
MEDIASOUP_RTC_MAX_PORT=40100
MEDIASOUP_PREFER_TCP=false
TURN_URLS=turn:localhost:3478
TURN_USERNAME=dimovie
TURN_CREDENTIAL=dimovie

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:4000/auth/google/callback
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
DISCORD_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:4000/auth/discord/callback
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRICE_ID=
```

## apps/web (.env.local)

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=DiMovie
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
```

## Railway (api service)

1. Add PostgreSQL + Redis plugins; wire `DATABASE_URL` and `REDIS_URL`.
2. Set JWT secrets, `CORS_ORIGIN` / `FRONTEND_URL` to the Vercel URL.
3. Leave `COOKIE_DOMAIN` empty if web proxies via `/backend`.
4. Configure R2 vars for uploads (bucket + public CDN URL).
5. Voice on Railway: keep `VOICE_SFU_ENABLED=false`. TURN works out of the box via Open Relay; override with `TURN_URLS` / `METERED_TURN_API_URL` for production volume.
6. SFU only on VPS/bare metal: `VOICE_SFU_ENABLED=true`, `MEDIASOUP_ANNOUNCED_IP=<public-ip>`, open UDP `MEDIASOUP_RTC_*` range.
7. Dockerfile installs Playwright Chromium for Rezka catalog; entrypoint runs `prisma migrate deploy`.
8. Healthcheck: `GET /health`.

## Local TURN (optional)

```bash
docker compose --profile voice up -d coturn
```

Then `TURN_URLS=turn:127.0.0.1:3478`, user/pass `dimovie`/`dimovie`.

## Vercel (web)

Root directory: `apps/web`.

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=DiMovie
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://YOUR-API.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=https://YOUR-API.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
```
